>
  <p>
    englishtoburmese.com is a free online translator built for people who need to move between English and Burmese (Myanmar) quickly. Whether you are studying, travelling, helping family, or working with documents, the site is meant to be simple and useful.
  </p>
  <h2>What you can translate</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Typed or pasted English text</li>
    <li>Spoken English via the Talk button, which fills the text box</li>
    <li>Documents in .txt, Word (.docx), and PDF format</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    English text is sent to a translation service and returned in Unicode Myanmar script. The Talk button uses the browser microphone so spoken English appears in the text box. Documents are opened on the server so the extracted text can be translated.
  </p>
  <h2>Our aim</h2>
  <p>
    We want a clean, public translator that does not require an account. Results are provided as a convenience and should be checked before use in legal, medical, academic, or official settings. See our <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a> and <a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a> for details.
  </p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions or feedback? Visit the <a href="/contact">Contact us</a> page.
  </p>
</Legal>
